{"id": "EUVD-2026-103786", "enisaUuid": "31e5dca7-e505-35f0-a4cf-25a7c757bf61", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsctp: check RCV_SHUTDOWN after the sendmsg connect wait\n\nsctp_wait_for_connect() drops the socket lock while it sleeps. An\nout-of-the-blue ABORT can then be processed from the socket backlog and\nunlink the association. If a concurrent shutdown(fd, SHUT_RD) sets\nRCV_SHUTDOWN, the waiter breaks with err == 0 before checking\nasoc->base.dead. Its final sctp_association_put() can then free the\nassociation, leaving sctp_sendmsg_to_asoc() to continue with a dangling\npointer.\n\nCheck RCV_SHUTDOWN along with the wait error in sctp_sendmsg_to_asoc()\nbefore using the association again. The check only accesses the socket,\nso it needs no additional association reference. Return the existing\n-ESRCH so that sctp_sendmsg() skips freeing a new association that may\nalready have been destroyed.\n\nKeep sctp_wait_for_connect() unchanged to preserve its behavior for the\nconnect() caller.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:50:34", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:26", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1bef1944ef15a40797305bf916827b04df6307ca", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e8f972b1759d26bbefe4c524caae1ed7c8a593bd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e701345d886e831fb593a0870d69c8c5de6fc938", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/222c41e0f50f1d5028be9baf0e1dcfc0bfa7f669", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4f1da630d13de0370e2f6361f961f1c8b384af1c"], "aliases": ["GHSA-gghw-9hqp-85hc", "CVE-2026-98846"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.16, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "20fd99a8-dd9a-3181-9906-d267a9b37495", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668c9beb9020d5834ee9e43c208190a07d2b1928 <e8f972b1759d26bbefe4c524caae1ed7c8a593bd"}, {"id": "2e14d566-7cef-313a-b5d0-7fa5c272983d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668c9beb9020d5834ee9e43c208190a07d2b1928 <222c41e0f50f1d5028be9baf0e1dcfc0bfa7f669"}, {"id": "343a2be8-d6f0-3a9b-ac7a-475fb3931e7b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "37c46e01-e5ea-3e7a-a180-050996b1eab3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668c9beb9020d5834ee9e43c208190a07d2b1928 <1bef1944ef15a40797305bf916827b04df6307ca"}, {"id": "397157f3-abb3-38ce-b16c-b313b128a823", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "7cf5c642-6e11-3257-88ed-f32a09bc1574", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "97993c6d-f971-3dd2-9173-3dbc84ad0faa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668c9beb9020d5834ee9e43c208190a07d2b1928 <e701345d886e831fb593a0870d69c8c5de6fc938"}, {"id": "bd4ddd9d-e4c1-355e-bbba-116f58511bb8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "668c9beb9020d5834ee9e43c208190a07d2b1928 <4f1da630d13de0370e2f6361f961f1c8b384af1c"}, {"id": "bff2e238-4926-3802-b95e-bcbf0423bd2b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.16"}, {"id": "c1cf493f-c56a-33a7-9a03-8d14158df3f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "e478abeb-4bc0-3f38-b955-30765d2595e5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "f96aadda-83e2-315c-bc0b-cbc471e41797", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "bd65b4bf-a8d7-30fe-bc70-a33d61a42b65", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}